+    // The fsopen()/fsconfig()/fsmount()/move_mount() mount API only exists on
+    // Linux >= 5.2.  ksuinit runs as the very first userspace process and must
+    // mount /proc itself before Android's init does (Android init mounts proc
+    // later, in first_stage_init).  On non-GKI 4.19 the new API returns ENOSYS,
+    // /proc stays unmounted, /proc/kallsyms cannot be read and init_module()
+    // fails, so kernelsu.ko never loads.  Use the classic mount(2) syscall,
+    // which works on every kernel we target (4.19 through GKI).
